        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eb9f51c0-28cc-574f-9478-bd87b72485c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zachariah T. Woodall\n- Organizations: U.S. Army, 6th U.S. Cavalry\n- Events: Red River War, Spanish–American War\n- Places: Southern Plains, Indian Territory\n- Topics: Native American forced relocation\n\nFacts:\n- The United States Army launched the Red River War in 1874 to remove the Comanche, Kiowa, Southern Cheyenne, and Arapaho tribes from the Southern Plains and forcibly relocate them to reservations in Indian Territory.\n- Zachariah T. Woodall was born in September 1849.\n- Zachariah T. Woodall was a soldier in the U.S. Army who served with the 6th U.S. Cavalry during the Red River War.\n- Zachariah T. Woodall later served during the Spanish–American War.\n- Zachariah T. Woodall died on September 12, 1899.",
